d down the epithets that  were that were thrown at the Utah  delegation it was hostile I mean it was  finger-pointing spittle from the mouth  very passionate and it was hatred  against the Utah for what they were  trying to do is for under what I think  stand by our principles my observation  is that there  - wings within the Republican Party I  call it the Jeffersonian wing and the  Roosevelt wing you've got two different  philosophies you know Roosevelt a  renowned progressive the in turn of the  century a very activist government trust  busters and Jefferson who is the the  Mentalist in the you know the the tree  of liberty is watered with the blood of  tyrants type  I think the worm has turned I believe  that that the Jeffersonian wing is now a  distinct distinct minority  I always referred to myself in the  legislature as a very small minority  within the majority party do you find  much support among your constituents for  Jeffersonian ideals or libertarian  ideals I know those are in some ways  separate things but related I represent  and the people I interact with have been  very supportive under understanding and  they've at least given me an opportunity  to try and explain my reasons why and  and after having had that opportunity  most of them even if they don't agree  they understand my issue is I thought  the Republican Party set stood for a  certain set of ideals and my frustration  was people who would paint themselves  red carry the Republican banner and and  take advantage of those set of ideals to  get elected and and used them  rhetorically and then never even think  about applying them to policy once they  got elected or there are other areas  besides you know gun rights the where  you feel like the Republican Party here  is falling short in terms of protecting  constitutional rights and civil  liberties I have an a rating with the  NRA now I also have an A rating with the  ACLU because I believe in all ten of the  Bill of Rights the surveillance 