 natural outcome of joining  another part it's a serious thing I've  been Republican forever do you think  there's any hope for libertarians in  Utah we're in a state that has highly  restrictive alcohol regulations let  alone marijuana that was yes another  very frustrating example of Utah being  out of step with other states that are  moving in a free the direction of  freedom conservative principles as far  as I see them and understand them and  that is lost on the majority of the  Republican representation in this state  the hypocrisy of people who call  themselves conservative and say how dare  Michelle Obama say I can't have salt on  my Big Mac okay fine  it is your life on your consequence but  they toggle off those  suppose when it's convenient or when  they think they know better and they say  oh we can't let people choose before it  between cannabis and opioids because why  do you think that there is a place going  forward for small-l libertarians such as  yourself or Rand Paul or maybe Mike  leaves some extent Justin Amash are  there gonna be more of those going  forward or as Trump totally demolished  that and as the libertarian army of the  future I speculate that Trump will weak  in the Republican Party post-election I  don't have a lot of confidence again in  either one of those two and their  ability to govern I think we're not in  great shape now as a country and I think  four years from now that may be the  critical moment we think things are bad  now four years from now maybe the time  the moment in history when when the  libertarians have to step up and save  the nation  ideally I'd love to have a couple of  people that that switch parties and form  a libertarian caucus and and follow  through and elect their own leadership  and have seats on the Appropriations  Committee and and establish themselves  as a legitimate minority party and  engage in policymaking here the  Democrats wield a lot of control when  you've got a bifurcated Republican Party  as I've described where you have the  Jeffersonian Roosevelt that you know  those Democrats can wield a lot of power  the minority party  can it can be the kingmaker the  Libertarian Party could have much the  same dynamic it could be a much sought  after a you know support group for  certain bills and again being inside  those rooms where those decisions are  made having an equal standing with the  other two parties would be huge

